Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Devon Gimbel  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 33 year old woman with a new cluster of calcifications seen on a recent mammogram  The patient s mother had breast cancer at age 36  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE WITH COMEDO NECROSIS  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Microscopic foci involving 1 of 6 blocks spanning at least 0 6cm  GRADE  2  CALCIFICATIONS  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer in areas of ductal carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm excision specimen with one needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is oriented per the surgeon as follows  Short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral  The long axis of the specimen is the superior inferior axis  and the specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal cut surfaces predominantly with gray tan  fibrous tissue with focal grittiness at the inferior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is submitted in toto from inferior to superior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the inferior margin en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the superior margin en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 21 CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass  stitch marks new deep margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN WITH LYMPHATIC AND PERINEURAL INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  SLIDE G   BREAST  LEFT  NEW DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   EXCISION  1  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE CONSISTING OF FIBROCIS  CYSTIC CHANGES  FOCAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  3  RADIAL SCAR  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The tumor displays some features of medullary carcinoma  focal dense lymphoid infiltrate and poorly differentiated nuclei   However  additional permanent sections display an infiltrative margin  glandular differentiation  and lack of syncitial formation which is diagnostic for a poorly differentiated carcinoma rather than a medullary carcinoma  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 39 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  MASS   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number in two parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of fibroadipose tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse  The deepest portion of the specimen is focally hard  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan  gritty mass that abuts the inked resection margin  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted as A  Representative portions of the tumor including the closest resection margin are submitted in B through E  A representative portion of the overlying skin is submitted in F  Representative portions of grossly unremarkable tissue is submitted in G through I  A gross photograph is taken  Labeled  new deep resection margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch marking the deepest portion  The deep margin is inked  the specimen is sectioned perpendicular to the long axis  and submitted entirely in J through N  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  POSSIBLY MEDULLARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  NEW DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
