Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right nipple duct excision  Rule out papilloma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT NIPPLE DUCT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1 TO FOCAL 2  WITH FOCUS HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR EARLY INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  One slightly irregular focus of carcinoma almost completely lacks a myoepithelial cell layer  as seen on p63  smooth muscle myosin  and calponin immunostains  A cytokeratin stain highlights the irregularities in contour  This area spans about 0 1cm and is favored to represent early blunt invasion arising out of ductal carcinoma in situ  Other nests of carcinoma also demonstrate large gaps in the myoepithelial cell layer  perhaps representing an earlier stage of the same phenomenon  The ductal carcinoma in situ involves 8 of 12 blocks and is focally positive at the inked margin  as well as being  0 1cm from the inked margin along a broad front  Calcifications are present in the ductal carcinoma in situ and in vessels  Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right nipple duct rule out papilloma   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm excisional breast biopsy specimen consisting of tan yellow  lobulated fatty tissue with focal hemorrhage externally  The specimen is not oriented  The external surface is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal somewhat firm  ill defined tissue in the central portion of the specimen distinct from the surrounding yellow  lobulated fatty  soft tissue  The ill defined region is somewhat firm and tan white  The ill defined region focally abuts the margin  One potential duct is identified 0 2cm in diameter  and multiple potential small ducts are identified which measures 0 1cm in diameter  The largest potential duct contains mucoid material  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ends of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue from central portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue containing ducts from central portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of specimen  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  No definitive invasive tumor cells are seen in the tissue sections for receptor stains   See note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT NIPPLE DUCT   EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 55 CLINICAL DATA  79 year old female with right breast cancer  Status post chemo x 5  Biopsy in REMOVED_DATE showed infiltrating ductal and lobular carcinoma with lobular carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2  RESIDUAL LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INFLAMMATORY REACTION TO SUTURE  CONSISTENT WITH SITE OF PREVIOUS SURGERY  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is present in the form of single cells and small aggregates of cells percolating through stroma in multiple areas throughout the breast  An estimation of the overall size of the tumor is difficult  but it spans at least 5cm  Infiltrating tumor extends to within 0 1cm of the deep inked surface  An immunoperoxidase stain for keratin confirms the presence of infiltrating carcinoma  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   AXILLARY DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IS PRESENT IN FOURTEEN OF SIXTEEN LYMPH NODES  EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION IS PRESENT  NOTE  An immunoperoxidase stain for keratin confirms the presence of metastatic carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 41 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast with some axillary contents  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a 3 0cm curved healed incision 3 0cm lateral to the unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm firm tan white mass with areas of white streaking and a granular gritty cut surface  approximately 1 6cm inferior to the incision and extending to 0 5cm of the deep inked margin  Approximately 4 0cm medial to the lesion is a firm white area approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  grossly abutting the inked deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma shows foci of firm white gritty tissue within areas of gray fibrous soft tissue  These areas of firm white gritty tissue are infiltrated with fat  The nipple is unremarkable  Multiple areas are sectioned and submitted as follows  Section Code  A  lesion  deep to scar  closest deep margin  0 5cm    B  lesion  C  lesion  D  lesion within 0 9cm of the deep margin  E  lesion  F G  firm white area abutting the inked deep margin  H  representative breast parenchyma  I J  fibrous area 2 0cm lateral to the lesion  K O  nodes from axillary tail  P  nodes and suspicious area in axillary tail  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  AND AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 24 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old with invasive ductal carcinoma on biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 16 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  The first part is designated  breast  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm piece of breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm skin ellipse attached  The cut surface is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  well demarcated cavity  The surrounding tissue is firm  white to yellow  with hemorrhagic areas  The cavity comes to within 0 4cm of the surface  Sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes A through F  Representative section of tissue away from the cavity are submitted in G and H  The second specimen is received fresh  and designated  right axillary tissue  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue and nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I through N  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART B  RIGHT BREAST  RE EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unch