Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 34 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  THREE FOCI RANGING FROM REMOVED_DATE TO REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  APOCRINE TYPE  EXTENDING THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND TO ITS MARGIN IN MANY FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  APOCRINE TYPE  INVOLVING DUCTS AND LOBULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO ITS MARGIN IN MANY FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FEW MICROSCOPIC FOCI  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  SMALL PAPILLOMAS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  1   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a specimen in three parts  Labeled  Right breast mass  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm breast tissue  with irregular hard areas throughout the specimen  which is entirely submitted in A J and BB GG  Labeled  Right breast mass  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue with multiple pinpoint yellow areas throughout the specimen  with some harder areas  No mass is identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K   V  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of breast tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hard nodular area  The specimen is submitted entirely in W   AA  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX 1 and 2  BREAST  RIGHT   1 AND  2   BIOPSIES  FIRM  POTENTIALLY ABNORMAL AREAS IN BOTH SPECIMENS  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DX  3  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FEW VERY SMALL  FIRM AREAS  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCE