ng from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm in greatest dimension  These lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left final shaved margin  lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented fragment of breast tissue  The surface is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fragmented breast tissue  which is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left beast final shaved margin  medial   is a single1 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented fragment of breast tissue  which is inked black  serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  inferior breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of breast tissue  The entirely specimen is inked black  serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do 