ns are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section between medial end and biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section around biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections corresponding to subsequent tissue sections  including slice marked by localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of tissue around biopsy cavity and area indicated by localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  Note  Essentially the entire biopsy site and the region bracketed by the wires corresponding to the region of interest have been submitted  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel tissue   are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue  measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  Five potential lymph nodes are identified in this tissue  Four potential lymph nodes are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One large lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL  456   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Abner Louissaint M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administr