 are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and tan irregular area from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue adjacent to intact wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm soft  tan yellow irregular portion of adipose tissue  On sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm lymph node  which has soft tan cut surfaces  The lymph node is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  1A  1B  1C  1D and 1E  The frozen section remnants are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional tissue at 2 o clock   stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal dense gray white fibrous tissue  which abuts the new margin  No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  1A 1B  1C  1D  1E  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagno