                                                                BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  tumor mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of breast tissue with a short stitch on the superior margin and a long stitch on the lateral margin  The entire specimen is inked black  the lateral side is overinked in blue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm  irregular white tan mass in the mid portion of the specimen  which is 0 5cm in the closest margin  medial   The remainder of the parenchyma is fatty and focally fibrous  Representative sections of this mass with the closest medial margin are submitted in A B  a representative section of tumor is submitted in C  and the tumor relative to the superior margin is submitted in D  A representative section of parenchyma distal to the lesion that is focally fibrous is submitted in E F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x1 3 x 0 5cm lymph node that is colored with blue dye  with a small amount of attached fat  The node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now in G  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  more superior sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node with a small amount of attached fatty tissue  The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 2  now in H  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  separate lateral mass   is a REMOVED_DATE 0 x 2 0cm aggregate of three pieces of breast tissue  which are unoriented  Within the largest piece  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm mass and a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm mass  both of which abut inked margins  One half of each nodule is frozen as fx 3  The remainder of the parenchyma is fatty with focally fibrous and rubbery areas  Frozen section  3 is now in I  The remainder of both nodules is submitted in J  Representative sections of the fibrous and rubbery areas are submitted in K L  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of tan yellow fatty tissue  inked  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes I and J  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  more inferior sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node surrounded by fatty tissue  bisected and submitted entirely in cassette K  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary contents   are multiple aggregates of fatty nodular tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  dissected for nodes which are submitted in cassette M  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  final shave margin   are three fragments of fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  inked  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes N  O  P and Q  Gross Description by  