Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  Lawerence R Zukerberg  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Christopher K Hysell  M D  Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Suspicious cytology  History of MALT lymphoma involving left breast and skin  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE TABLE  1   MULTIFOCAL PERIDUCTAL ATYPICAL LYMPHOPLASMACYTIC INFILTRATE WITH FOCAL PERIDUCTAL AMYLOID DEPOSITION  CONSISTENT WITH MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SEE NOTE   Note  There is a dense periductal and perilobular atypical lymphoid infiltrate throughout the breast composed of small mature appearing lymphocytes with abundant pale cytoplasm and numerous plasma cells  There are frequent lymphoepithelial lesions and scattered Dutcher bodies  The morphologic features are identical to those of the previously diagnosed marginal zone B cell lymphoma in the left breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The immunophenotype of the infiltrate has been previously determined and is not repeated here  Results of a Congo red stain confirm the presence of focal periductal amyloid deposition  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  0 9cm  slide measurement   Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma 