ree  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION  1  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION  1  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION  1  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION  1  FAT NECROSIS  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  Sally Quigley  REMOVE_MRN  right breast lumpectomy with two needle localization wires in place  long lateral  short superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm oriented breast tissue  with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is received with blue green inked discoloration of the anterior superior surface  The specimen is additionally inked as follows  superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm  ill defined  white tan mass in the mid portion of the specimen  0 6cm from the superior margin  1 2cm from the inferior margin  1 4cm from the medial margin  0 9cm from lateral margin  2 3cm from the anterior margin  and 1 7cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the specimen consists of fatty breast parenchyma with focal hemorrhage surrounding the second localization wire  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest superior and lateral margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest inferior margin  region of clip    