ill not be seen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The most lateral part of the specimen appears unremarkable  and the entire specimen is not submitted  The entire nodule is submitted however  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   medial posterior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm dome shaped soft tissue specimen with a stitch placed by the surgeon denoting the plane of the new margin  The new margin is inked black  This new margin does have an area of fibrous white tissue on part of its surface  Underlying the inked margin there is yellowish fatty tissue with interspersed white fibrous tissue  This specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The majority   90   of the specimen is submitted  Gross Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL POSTERIOR MARGIN   E