stration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a modified radical mastectomy consisting of a right breast  measuring 15 x 12 x 1 5cm  a overlying nipple and areola  The areola measures 3 x 2 x 0 6cm and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Due to fixation artifact  the previous excisional biopsy scar in not identified  The posterior margin is inked black  The anterior margin is inked red and the specimen is bread loaf to reveal a 2 x 2 x 1cm firm lesion  On cut section the lesion is white lobulated and glistening  The lesion also has two focal areas of yellow parenchyma  suggestive of possible fat necrosis   The lesion is located  0 1cm from the deep margin  The lesion is also located deep and superior to the nipple  SECTION CODE A F  Lesions G H  Fibrous area inferior to nipple I  Deep margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary content  is a 5 x 4 x 1 7cm fragment of adipose tissue  The specimen was dissected and several lymph nodes identified  SECTION CODE J  3 lymph nodes K  5 lymph nodes L  7 lymph nodes M  3 lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  additional right axillary content  is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue submitted in its entirety in cassette N  Resident  KENNETH HARRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  Paula Denise Ryan  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   MODIFIED RADICAL MAST PART C  LYM