at stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  and designated as  L breast  stitch superior   is a 30 x 17 x 5 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and a 4 0cm linear scar  8cm lateral to the nipple  A stitch designates the superior aspect of the specimen  The attached axillary tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Deep to the skin scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity surrounded by a rim of ill defined tan yellow  fibrous tissue  It abuts the overlying skin and is 0 8cm from the nearest deep resection margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined tan white rubbery area located 4 0cm lateral to the biopsy cavity  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  The axillary nodes range in size from 0 4cm to 1 7cm in greatest diameter and are rubbery and tan pink  Section Code  A  cavity with skin margin B  deep margin C E  representative sections of the mass F H  nodular areas I and J  axillary nodes Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
