Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 43 year old woman with a strong family history of breast cancer and a history of invasive ductal carcinoma in the right breast undergoing bilateral mastectomy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1   3  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  1 2    SEE TABLE  2   4  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Five microscopic foci  0 5  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE and 0 15cm   present adjacent to the healing biopsy site  GRADE  2 MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to  0 1cm from the superior and posterior margins of the specimen in two foci  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to 0 1cm from the superior margin of the specimen in one focus  NOTE  An immunostain for e cadherin performed on slide A 10 is pending and will be reported in an addendum  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  2 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  3  LACTATIONAL CHANGE  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right simple mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm area of skin containing the nipple present on the anterior surface  and the specimen oriented with a stitch at 12 o clock  The anterior soft tissue margin shows focal scarring in the REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area in the right lateral portion of the breast  2 0cm from the right lateral margin  The posterior surface of the breast shows primarily unremarkable fibroadipose tissue and thin fascia  but also shows a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of mild fibrous thickening in the right lateral aspect  2 0cm from the right lateral margin  The anterior soft tissue is inked blue and the posterior soft tissue is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm cystic and hemorrhagic prior resection cavity with focal firm nodular yellow areas in the immediately surrounding tissue  This cavity lies 0 2cm from the deep and 0 6cm from the anterior soft tissue margins  and extends to 1 2cm from the right lateral margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is primarily fibrous within approximately 4 0cm of the nipple and primarily adipose elsewhere  The superior right lateral quadrant is carefully examined for lymph nodes and two are identified with the larger measuring 0 9cm in greatest diameter and having a heterogenous pink and firm  tan white cut surface  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral aspect of resection cavity to superior and inferior margins  one section    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One cross section of the resection cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section through resection cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of resection cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous area deep to nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Right upper quadrant lymph nodes  two  one blue inked and bisected  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating 6 o clock and a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of skin present anteriorly and containing the nipple  The anterior soft tissue surface consists of unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue and the posterior resection surface consists of unremarkable breast tissue and thin fascia  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal primarily adipose breast parenchyma with an area of primarily fibrous tissue inferiorly  The fibrous area around the nipple also contains focal brown cystic nodules up to 0 2cm  There is also a fairly discrete REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrous area in the left lateral superior portion of the specimen  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous areas in left lateral superior quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous area in left lateral inferior quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fibrous area in inferior portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from medial inferior quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section deep to nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of medial portion of specimen  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin  performed on slide A 10 confirms the diagnosis of lobular neoplasia  lobular carcinoma in situ  in this section  Addendum  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Unchecked.
