r approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an overlying piece of skin including nipple  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and showing a peripheral 5 5cm linear healed scar  The nipple appears unremarkable  The specimen also includes a portion of axillary tail  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The surgical margins are inked in black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity  located beneath the scar and occupying the midportion of the specimen  The cavity wall comes focally to within 0 2cm from the posterior resection margin and is filled with a soft and somewhat necrotic pink red material  The surrounding breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail is dissected and multiple lymph nodes are identified  The largest lymph node  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  is grossly involved by tumor  A second large lymph node is also grossly involved by tumor  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A B  Closest deep resection margin  C  Cavity and anterior resection margin  D F  Cavity wall  G  Nipple  H  Overlying skin including scar  I  Normal breast  medial to cavity  J  Largest lymph node  grossly involved by tumor  one half  K  Lymph node  grossly involved by tumor  one half  L  Two lymph nodes  bisected  M  One lymph node  trisected  N O  Multiple lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm